A maintainer on the project BabySid/aether (Go) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #1: Loop with zero resolved items deadlocks the parent workflow

# Loop with zero resolved items deadlocks the parent workflow (and, if naively fixed, can corrupt sibling task state)

## Summary

When a `loop` template's `items`/`itemsFrom` resolves to an empty array, `startLoopController`'s zero-iteration branch (`engine_loop.go`, "3. Zero iterations: mark the loop as succeeded immediately") marks the Loop's own `TaskRun` `Succeeded` but never notifies its parent scope. The Loop node itself shows `Succeeded`, but the DAG containing it never advances past it — the workflow hangs in `Running` forever, with no error, no timeout (unless an explicit task-level timeout is set on something downstream), nothing.

Confirmed against `main` @ `002e3b7eedf9b16b83d54b0f69cb121293a5a614` (current HEAD as of filing).

This isn't a corner case — a Loop resolving to zero items is a completely ordinary outcome (e.g. `itemsFrom` filtering a runtime list down to nothing, or a user-driven "process only the items I selected, and I selected none").

## Repro

Save as `cmd/playground/examples/31-loop-empty-items.json` (written to match the existing `06-loop-static.json` / `07-loop-aggregate.json` style):

```json
{
    "apiVersion": "aether/v1",
    "kind": "Workflow",
    "metadata": {
        "name": "loop-empty-items",
        "annotations": {
            "description": "Loop whose itemsFrom/items resolves to zero items: the DAG containing it should still advance to downstream tasks, the same way it would if every item were simply processed. It doesn't.",
            "test:expect-phase": "Succeeded",
            "test:expect-task-count": "3"
        }
    },
    "spec": {
        "entrypoint": "pipeline",
        "templates": [
            {
                "dag": {
                    "name": "pipeline",
                    "tasks": [
                        { "name": "batch", "template": "empty-loop" },
                        {
                            "name": "consumer",
                            "template": "collect",
                            "dependencies": ["batch"],
                            "arguments": {
                                "parameters": [
                                    { "name": "scores", "valueFrom": { "parameter": "tasks.batch.outputs.parameters.score" } }
                                ]
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                }
            },
            {
                "loop": {
                    "name": "empty-loop",
                    "items": [],
                    "body": "score-item",
                    "aggregate": { "strategy": "list", "parameters": ["score"] },
                    "outputs": { "parameters": [ { "name": "score", "type": "array" } ] }
                }
            },
            {
                "task": {
                    "name": "score-item",
                    "inputs": { "parameters": [ { "name": "item", "type": "string" } ] },
                    "executor": { "type": "echo" },
                    "outputs": { "parameters": [ { "name": "score", "type": "int" } ] }
                }
            },
            {
                "task": {
                    "name": "collect",
                    "inputs": {
                        "parameters": [
                            { "name": "scores", "type": "array" },
                            {
                                "name": "outputs",
                                "value": [ { "name": "received", "type": "bool", "value": true } ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "executor": { "type": "echo" },
                    "outputs": { "parameters": [ { "name": "received", "type": "bool" } ] }
                }
            }
        ]
    }
}
```

```
go build -o playground ./cmd/playground
./playground -workflow cmd/playground/examples/31-loop-empty-items.json -timeout 30
```

**Expected**: workflow reaches `Succeeded`, task count 3 (`pipeline`, `batch` (the loop), `consumer`), `batch.outputs.score == []`, `consumer` runs and receives that empty array.

**Actual**: `batch` (the Loop) shows `Succeeded` with `Message: "loop had no iterations"`, but `pipeline` (its parent DAG) stays `Running` indefinitely and `consumer` is never even created. The playground run has to be killed by its own `-timeout`.

## Root cause

Two separate problems in the same branch, `engine_loop.go`, `startLoopController`, "3. Zero iterations":

```go
if len(iterations) == 0 {
    succeeded := model.PhaseSucceeded
    noIterMsg := "loop had no iterations"
    _, err = e.store.UpdateTaskRun(ctx, &store.TaskRun{
        RunID:   loopTR.RunID,
        Token:   loopTR.Token,
        Status:  &succeeded,
        Message: &noIterMsg,
    })
    return err
}
```

